# ── Counterfactual: the unguarded pen AND the kept conjuncts stripped ────────
# The arming case for its two siblings, and it exists because neither of them
# can arm itself. `unguarded-pen` adds a credential route that forgets
# ~match(·, CarriedVoid) and ~broken, then shows the void still failing —
# which proves the multi-sig's own copies of those guards are doing the work
# only if they are the last thing standing. `no-dead-conjuncts` strips the
# guards, then shows chapters 24 and 25 unmoved — which proves they are
# subsumed only while some other rule still catches what they catch.
#
# Here both changes are applied at once, so nothing catches a carried-void
# signer. If this file ever reads FALSE, the pair above has gone vacuous and
# the justification for keeping four conjuncts in Article 4 has gone with it.
:expect-pins 4

# Vex was voided in a prior period. The added route seats him anyway.
? permits(Review, Vex).
# => TRUE

? permits(Tribunal, Wren).
# => TRUE

# Both signers hold case-bound independence findings for Tyr and cite the same
# recorded ground, so every other condition of the void is met and the four
# stripped conjuncts are the only difference from the shipped file.
? match(Vex, CarriedVoid).
# => TRUE

# And a signer whose own word is worthless destroys a stranger's.
? false(Tyr).
# => TRUE
